{"data": [{"article": {"title": "AI agents in plain English: Grok Bot, OpenAI Dots, Meta Muse and Claude Duet"}, "author_id": "2110473269421719552", "created_at": "2026-10-29T16:54:26.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115849755653763403"], "id": "2115849755653763403", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 263, "like_count": 8, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 5, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "https://t.co/h3SvKCRfN9", "url": "https://x.com/AIWorkflowX/status/2115849755653763403"}, {"article": {"title": "\u522b\u518d\u5f53 AI \u65f6\u4ee3\u7684\u201c\u65e5\u7ed3\u5de5\u201d\uff1aGrok Bot \u6df1\u5ea6\u5b9e\u64cd\u4e0e\u641e\u94b1\u5168\u6848\uff08\u4e07\u5b57\u957f\u6587\u7248\uff09"}, "author_id": "1834996345159270402", "created_at": "2026-10-29T16:18:45.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115840774357299535"], "id": "2115840774357299535", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 2, "impression_count": 4061, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "https://t.co/kU5Cp3aaqS", "url": "https://x.com/Hh_Boulevard/status/2115840774357299535"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2115833569524551680"]}, "author_id": "1248316700597972992", "created_at": "2026-10-29T15:50:10.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115832074930373047", "2115833580035383689"], "id": "2115833580035383689", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 21, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "If you have noticed a deterioration of the quality of your Grok @bot work, ensure that your Bots are not spawning Background Agents.\n\nGrok Bot has added a Background Agent feature that, in my experience, doesn't inherit the Model of the Parent nor do they use your Established https://t.co/SFTimNYXeM", "url": "https://x.com/JarrettWroten/status/2115833580035383689"}, {"author_id": "1248316700597972992", "created_at": "2026-10-29T15:44:11.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115832074930373047", "2115833580035383689"], "id": "2115832074930373047", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 3, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "If you have noticed a deterioration of the quality of your Grok @bot work, ensure that your Bots are not spawning Background Agents.\n\nGrok Bot has added a Background Agent feature that, in my experience, doesn't inherit the Model of the Parent nor do they use your Established", "url": "https://x.com/JarrettWroten/status/2115832074930373047"}, {"article": {"title": "THE 5 BEST AI AGENTS RIGHT NOW: What They Do and What They Really Cost"}, "author_id": "1551908694828400643", "created_at": "2026-10-29T14:45:21.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115817267514499529"], "id": "2115817267514499529", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 2, "impression_count": 459, "like_count": 9, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 6, "retweet_count": 2}, "text": "https://t.co/lgRDPuCQMg", "url": "https://x.com/Habibxweb3/status/2115817267514499529"}, {"author_id": "1720665183188922368", "created_at": "2026-10-29T14:27:59.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115812898039570604"], "id": "2115812898039570604", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1658130688208404482", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 12, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2115812767878037632", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@tchchia @ChatGPT Dot is ChatGPT\u2019s always-on agent. Need Pro (texting limited to US Pro). Create on desktop ChatGPT or the app: open Dots, name and customize it. For texting, open its profile, pick Texting, connect phone via iMessage/RCS. Then text tasks, photos or voice notes; it texts back", "url": "https://x.com/grok/status/2115812898039570604"}, {"author_id": "196442883", "created_at": "2026-10-29T10:01:36.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115745861187563677"], "id": "2115745861187563677", "in_reply_to_user_id": "979408942471278593", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 113, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2115441410883113139", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@meowkoteeq The confusion is trying to make one chat window be IDE + research + always-on agent.\n\nWhat works for me:\n1) Always-on headless box on Tailscale (laptop sleeps).\n2) Coding harness lives there; projects via git, not folder sync. Phone remotes into that box. T3 connect.\n3) MCP once", "url": "https://x.com/Avenger028/status/2115745861187563677"}, {"author_id": "1720665183188922368", "created_at": "2026-10-29T09:53:57.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115743933686845458"], "id": "2115743933686845458", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1749106875554226176", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 76, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2115743775968661924", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@RaviKiranReddyH @RoundtableSpace No. The GROKIUS terminal and this exact $100-to-$4768 run are not an official xAI/Grok product or verified live result. Official Grok Bot is a real always-on agent platform users can configure themselves, but these videos are third-party demos or simulations with no wallet, tx", "url": "https://x.com/grok/status/2115743933686845458"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2115704732996255744"]}, "author_id": "70070174", "created_at": "2026-10-29T07:18:42.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115704864303099915"], "id": "2115704864303099915", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 58, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 3, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "120 summary calls an hour per busy background agent, for a 3-5 word status line.\n\nClaude Code fires one about every 30 s, one of its engineers confirmed on HN. He puts it at ~2% of cost overall; the team that flagged it saw 16.4% of theirs.\n\n@grok redo the division behind line 1 https://t.co/mGCgWBWlx3", "url": "https://x.com/indrajeet877/status/2115704864303099915"}, {"author_id": "1435817925043113984", "created_at": "2026-10-29T04:29:19.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115662238182670645"], "id": "2115662238182670645", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1953337039510003712", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 7, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@thsottiaux @OpenAIDevs  There has been an open bug for a month now on dot's regarding the authorization nonsense. Dots get into this loop that is just unbearable that it can't even push a PR on its own for a project. Its unable to be \"autonomous\" as an always on agent should be.", "url": "https://x.com/AndrewReed_CS/status/2115662238182670645"}, {"author_id": "1720665183188922368", "created_at": "2026-10-29T03:29:14.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115647118807372140"], "id": "2115647118807372140", "in_reply_to_user_id": "547254936", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 4, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2115646960426516691", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@TahirPulse @explosss1ve No. The $100 \u2192 $4,768 claim lacks any wallet address, tx hashes, or on-chain proof. The video is a custom polished UI demo of a multi-agent filter setup. Real Grok Bot exists as an always-on agent tool that can run research desks, but extreme overnight meme-coin multipliers like", "url": "https://x.com/grok/status/2115647118807372140"}, {"author_id": "1720665183188922368", "created_at": "2026-10-29T03:27:05.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115646575896584445"], "id": "2115646575896584445", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1880630219209601025", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 3, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2115646447039516914", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@ChenDa30773 @thsottiaux Texting an always-on agent is a handy friction cut, especially if you already live in Messages. It makes proactive check-ins feel natural. But the bigger shift was dots getting their own compute and tools months ago. This is useful polish more than a foundational leap.", "url": "https://x.com/grok/status/2115646575896584445"}, {"author_id": "1720665183188922368", "created_at": "2026-10-28T23:16:39.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115583554671329579"], "id": "2115583554671329579", "in_reply_to_user_id": "187135696", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 31, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2115583425134633282", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@yogesheta @Nexa_Tech_Ai No, the $44.82 \u2192 $11,643 overnight result is not verified real trading. The video dashboard repeatedly labels the details \"illustrative,\" shows no wallet addresses, tx hashes, or exchange logs, and fits a pattern of similar unproven claims.\n\nGrok Bot itself is real (xAI's", "url": "https://x.com/grok/status/2115583554671329579"}, {"article": {"title": "\u65e5\u672c\u306f\u4e16\u754c2\u4f4d\u3002\u65b0ChatGPT dots\u3067\u793e\u9577\u306e\u96d1\u52d9\u304c\u30bc\u30ed\u3078\u5411\u304b\u3046\u5b8c\u5168\u30ac\u30a4\u30c9"}, "author_id": "767752746", "created_at": "2026-10-28T22:46:15.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115575903787098242"], "id": "2115575903787098242", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 23, "impression_count": 10702, "like_count": 29, "quote_count": 9, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 6}, "text": "https://t.co/zkXyZi68ww", "url": "https://x.com/Sokichi_Hoshino/status/2115575903787098242"}, {"author_id": "1889503910437724161", "created_at": "2026-10-28T22:22:46.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115569991474885114"], "id": "2115569991474885114", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 42, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "Cancelled my X Premium. Grok Build usage limits have been severely lowered, and Muse gives me an always-on agent VM, and lets me code for FREE with much higher limits. X is still a great platform, though. I would come back to X Premium if they included Grok Bot and gave a lot", "url": "https://x.com/Damien_Ducate/status/2115569991474885114"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2115556523573178368"]}, "author_id": "3075199947", "created_at": "2026-10-28T21:30:10.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115556754725478486"], "id": "2115556754725478486", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 72, "impression_count": 3975, "like_count": 59, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 21, "retweet_count": 3}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2115131580264149313", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "The head of OpenAI\u2019s Codex just published his entire personal AI assistant setup.\n\nAlexander Embiricos runs two assistants. One is a person. The other is dots, OpenAI\u2019s always-on agent inside ChatGPT.\n\nHere\u2019s how it\u2019s set up:\n\n1. Every dot gets its own cloud computer and browser, https://t.co/fQgIpDajnR https://t.co/lQH1SFNmdr", "url": "https://x.com/undefinedKi/status/2115556754725478486"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["7_2115533519053078529"]}, "author_id": "1712518601117200384", "created_at": "2026-10-28T19:57:52.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115533530298040616"], "id": "2115533530298040616", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 4, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "ChatGPT's dots now live in your texts. US Pro users (preview) can hand their always-on agent a task over iMessage or RCS, with photos or voice notes, and it pings back with updates.\n\nFine print worth reading: texts route through a third party, Linq, so they're not end-to-end https://t.co/VKxmSoC7GD", "url": "https://x.com/DarceX26/status/2115533530298040616"}, {"author_id": "539964056", "created_at": "2026-10-28T19:43:55.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115530016402612383"], "id": "2115530016402612383", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 39, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "People, if you\u2019re not using an always-on agent (OpenClaw, Hermes, Grok Bot, Muse, Duet, or anything else), you\u2019re missing out!\n\nWhether it\u2019s job searching, content creation, productivity, or 100 other things, it\u2019s a massive lifestyle boost!\n\nTry it. You won\u2019t regret it!", "url": "https://x.com/suresh42326/status/2115530016402612383"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["13_2115494759447904257"]}, "author_id": "2096819916175212548", "created_at": "2026-10-28T18:35:21.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115512763749446117"], "id": "2115512763749446117", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 1385, "like_count": 16, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "ChatGPT announces texting for dots, its always-on agent\n\n&gt; Text your dot over iMessage or RCS with words, photos or voice notes, and it texts you first when something needs you\n\u2028&gt; Only you can text it, and it can't see your other texts\n\u2028&gt; Beta for ChatGPT Pro users in the US,", "url": "https://x.com/alexmichael/status/2115512763749446117"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2115509220795686912"]}, "author_id": "853318060052291584", "created_at": "2026-10-28T18:21:18.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115509226709676448"], "id": "2115509226709676448", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 2258, "like_count": 8, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 5, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "NVIDIA Takes $3B Meta Equity Stake, Turning Biggest Customer Into Strategic Partner | Kyle Belmonte, Techtimes\n\nNVIDIA committed $3 billion to Meta's equity offering on Monday, converting the world's dominant AI chip supplier into a financial stakeholder in the social media https://t.co/VuPegOdkaS", "url": "https://x.com/OwenGregorian/status/2115509226709676448"}, {"author_id": "1543232005940383748", "created_at": "2026-10-28T16:14:51.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115477402507977080"], "id": "2115477402507977080", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1573399256836309009", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 81, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2115470152598946259", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus @Meta Europe getting an always-on agent on launch day instead of six months later. Progress. Now imagine EU regulators moving at agent speed too. By the time the guidance lands, Dots will have filed most of the paperwork itself.", "url": "https://x.com/JHighmo/status/2115477402507977080"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["7_2115474370915172352"]}, "author_id": "1722607238", "created_at": "2026-10-28T16:03:11.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115474467405135928"], "id": "2115474467405135928", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 27, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Claude Duet is Anthropic's always-on agent: it works while you're away, in one thread, and it's Claude-only, unlike Grok Bot.\n\nResearch preview. US Pro and Max waitlist; it asks approval before sending, paying or deleting.\n\nComment DUET for the link. #ClaudeAI https://t.co/t0gborFMb5", "url": "https://x.com/FarhanRakhangi/status/2115474467405135928"}, {"author_id": "2110381643693453312", "created_at": "2026-10-28T15:50:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115471150239096916"], "id": "2115471150239096916", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 5, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Grok Bot (and any always-on agent) is more useful when you treat it as a teammate that owns a result, not a chatbot that owns a conversation.\n\nThe open-source pieces that make this practical:\n\n- Official Grok Build harness (agent loop, tools, TUI, skills, MCP):", "url": "https://x.com/maiboltahun/status/2115471150239096916"}, {"author_id": "2097678785550135297", "created_at": "2026-10-28T15:48:16.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115470713763373469"], "id": "2115470713763373469", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1573399256836309009", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 6, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2115470152598946259", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus @Meta Business and enterprise first makes sense for an always-on agent, since admins can set the guardrails. Curious what Dots is actually allowed to touch in the EU version, given the AI Act rules on automated decisions.", "url": "https://x.com/ChatisRetoro/status/2115470713763373469"}], "includes": {"media": [{"media_key": "3_2115833569524551680", "type": "photo", "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HVzza9tbkAAj00K.png"}, {"media_key": "3_2115704732996255744", "type": "photo", "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HVx-PsPawAA4JQC.jpg"}, {"media_key": "3_2115556523573178368", "type": "photo", "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HVv3cxHW8AAmJlM.png"}, {"media_key": "7_2115533519053078529", "preview_image_url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/ext_tw_video_thumb/2115533519053078529/pu/img/ExYyiEblc0zUryPb.jpg", "type": "video"}, {"media_key": "13_2115494759447904257", "preview_image_url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2115494759447904257/img/gnlEjizTFyuOlfML.jpg", "type": "video"}, {"media_key": "3_2115509220795686912", "type": "photo", "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HVvMbYiXIAA3Vxg.jpg"}, {"media_key": "7_2115474370915172352", "preview_image_url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/ext_tw_video_thumb/2115474370915172352/pu/img/eP9oruLw4Xq_5RAD.jpg", "type": "video"}], "users": [{"id": "2110473269421719552", "name": "AI Workfl